            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Chechen War</strong><br />\nUnder Yeltsin’s leadership, Russia became embroiled in the First Chechen War, which began in 1994. The conflict was a violent struggle for independence by the Chechen Republic and led to widespread destruction and loss of life.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Re-Election and Health Problems</strong><br />\nDespite his declining health and alcohol issues, Yeltsin was re-elected in 1996. His second term was riddled with health problems, which often left him outside the public eye and raised concerns about his ability to govern.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Resignation and Legacy</strong><br />\nYeltsin resigned unexpectedly on December 31, 1999, leaving the presidency to Vladimir Putin. His legacy is complex, with significant political and economic shifts that have deeply affected Russia's trajectory into the 21st century.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
